# Phase Three — Final Plan Before Source Writes

The Awtsmoos makes the final plan a covenant of evidence, not a guess in disguise;
Awtsmoos.com will rewrite only files whose runtime ownership is proven before our eyes.

## Next reads

- boot/cache entrypoint;
- sticky visibility controller;
- mobile import graph;
- platform mount caller;
- tests covering Living Path and mobile shell.

## Expected source changes, pending those reads

1. Cache/version entrypoint: guarantee users receive the current Living Path/Chitas module graph.
2. Living Path context controller/discovery renderer: make Nearby Branches active-view aware and repaint on view changes.
3. Platform mobile CSS: inline collapsed Advanced on narrow screens instead of fixed overlay.
4. Mobile shell/Living Path CSS: reduce empty-space geometry and reserve one clean bottom-nav clearance.
5. Focused regression tests: Chitas grouping visibility/count, discovery view policy, mobile non-fixed Advanced contract, and source line limits.

## Verification order

- focused Node tests;
- existing Living Path/module tests;
- `node --check` on every touched JS;
- CSS static contract checks;
- `git diff --check`;
- full readback of every touched file;
- public HTTP/hash check of entrypoint and changed modules;
- browser-level verification if browser control becomes available; otherwise public HTML/module evidence plus user-visible test URL.
